[2026-03-14T21:45:51.487Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GFfT1QMkJy1rNNhd2rF7J9","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Documentation\n\n**Replay CLI** is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Users can record sessions, upload them, and manage recordings through command-line commands.\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nCreate an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and save it to the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launch Replay Browser and record a session\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Upload recordings (returns a viewable URL)\n- **`replayio list`** - List local recordings with status\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Delete recordings\n- **`replayio login/logout`** - Manage account access\n- **`replayio info`** - Display CLI and browser version info\n\n## Core Workflow\n\nRecord a session, then upload it:\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n## MCP Integration\n\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude to debug recorded applications using your `REPLAY_API_KEY` for authorization."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8ef0c01-5338-4db1-a807-d3d6ec6d21f8","uuid":"03806063-47cb-46a3-a77b-e940b99c090a","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Documentation\n\n**Replay CLI** is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Users can record sessions, upload them, and manage recordings through command-line commands.\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nCreate an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and save it to the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launch Replay Browser and record a session\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Upload recordings (returns a viewable URL)\n- **`replayio list`** - List local recordings with status\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Delete recordings\n- **`replayio login/logout`** - Manage account access\n- **`replayio info`** - Display CLI and browser version info\n\n## Core Workflow\n\nRecord a session, then upload it:\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n## MCP Integration\n\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude to debug recorded applications using your `REPLAY_API_KEY` for authorization.","durationMs":3197,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-14T21:45:53.097Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CUooSe8FtumnwfyEoKvr3n","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Documentation Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool designed to inspect recordings from https://replay.io, which capture complete browser execution data. As stated in the documentation, users can \"explore and investigate the app's behavior as if you are a detective with a time machine.\"\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nThe system organizes recorded data around two main concepts:\n\n**Points** represent specific moments in app execution, created whenever JavaScript statements run or significant events occur. **Elements** are persistent references to DOM objects that exist throughout portions of the recording.\n\n## Available Tools\n\nThe documentation categorizes tools into two primary groups:\n\n**Exploratory tools** help discover what happened and when, including error detection, timeline analysis, and source code examination. These range from identifying uncaught exceptions to reviewing console messages and network activity.\n\n**Explanatory tools** clarify why events occurred, offering stack traces, dependency analysis, and detailed state inspection at specific execution moments.\n\n## Recommended Approach\n\nThe guide emphasizes a structured investigation method: frame questions clearly, use exploratory tools to identify relevant events, employ explanatory tools to understand causation, develop hypotheses supported by gathered evidence, and communicate conclusions with data backing.\n\nThe Logpoint tool receives particular emphasis for tracking expression values across multiple executions, helping identify unexpected behavior patterns during debugging sessions."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8ef0c01-5338-4db1-a807-d3d6ec6d21f8","uuid":"eb9fb926-76a9-406a-bff4-ab71a1c1de01","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Documentation Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool designed to inspect recordings from https://replay.io, which capture complete browser execution data. As stated in the documentation, users can \"explore and investigate the app's behavior as if you are a detective with a time machine.\"\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nThe system organizes recorded data around two main concepts:\n\n**Points** represent specific moments in app execution, created whenever JavaScript statements run or significant events occur. **Elements** are persistent references to DOM objects that exist throughout portions of the recording.\n\n## Available Tools\n\nThe documentation categorizes tools into two primary groups:\n\n**Exploratory tools** help discover what happened and when, including error detection, timeline analysis, and source code examination. These range from identifying uncaught exceptions to reviewing console messages and network activity.\n\n**Explanatory tools** clarify why events occurred, offering stack traces, dependency analysis, and detailed state inspection at specific execution moments.\n\n## Recommended Approach\n\nThe guide emphasizes a structured investigation method: frame questions clearly, use exploratory tools to identify relevant events, employ explanatory tools to understand causation, develop hypotheses supported by gathered evidence, and communicate conclusions with data backing.\n\nThe Logpoint tool receives particular emphasis for tracking expression values across multiple executions, helping identify unexpected behavior patterns during debugging sessions.","durationMs":3696,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
